---
import DocsLayout from "../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import PageBody from "../components/PageBody.astro";
import Section from "../components/Section.astro";
import Code from "../components/Code.astro";
import { defineSections } from "../lib/sections";
import { route } from "../lib/catalogue";

const S = defineSections([
  { id: "footer", label: "Footer", heading: false },
  { id: "sticky-footer", label: "Sticky footer" },
]);
---
<DocsLayout page="footer">
<PageBody sections={S}>
  <Section {...S.footer}>
        <p class="flow-text">
          Use the footer for site navigation and extra information. People look there after they finish a page, or when they want to know more about the site.
        </p>
        <p>
          Put the page in the three HTML5 landmarks <code>header</code>, <code>main</code>, and <code>footer</code>.
          The footer is CSS only, with no JavaScript component. A
          <code>&lt;footer&gt;</code> whose only child is a
          <code>nav.navigation-bar</code> is the
          <a href={route('navigation_bar')}>navigation bar</a>.
          Anything richer is the site footer. Inside it, a heading is a column
          title, a <code>&lt;nav&gt;</code> is a link list, and the last
          <code>&lt;small&gt;</code> is the legal bar.
        </p>
        <p>
          By default the footer is unfilled, with a dashed hairline and theme
          tokens instead of a solid primary bar. Add <code>filled</code> (or <code>surface</code>) for a
          <code>surface-container</code> well.
        </p>

        <footer>
          <section>
            <h2>Product</h2>
            <p>A column with no links is not navigation — it is a section with a heading.</p>
          </section>
          <nav aria-labelledby="demo-footer-links">
            <h2 id="demo-footer-links">Links</h2>
            <a href="#!">Link 1</a>
            <a href="#!">Link 2</a>
            <a href="#!">Link 3</a>
            <a href="#!">Link 4</a>
          </nav>
          <small>
            <span>&copy; 2026 Copyright Text</span>
            <a href="#!">More Links</a>
          </small>
        </footer>

<Code code={`
<footer>
  <section>
    <h2>Product</h2>
    <p>A column with no links is not navigation — it is a section with a heading.</p>
  </section>
  <nav aria-labelledby="footer-links">
    <h2 id="footer-links">Links</h2>
    <a href="/link-1">Link 1</a>
    <a href="/link-2">Link 2</a>
  </nav>
  <small>
    <span>&copy; 2026 Copyright Text</span>
    <a href="/sitemap">More Links</a>
  </small>
</footer>
`} />
        <p>
          You can still use the grid if you prefer columns. The component is a
          bare <code>&lt;footer&gt;</code> with <code>&lt;nav&gt;</code> columns
          and a trailing <code>&lt;small&gt;</code>. <code>.page-footer</code> and
          <code>.footer-copyright</code> are <strong>not</strong> aliases, and no
          rule in the stylesheet matches either class.
        </p>
<Code code={`
<footer>
  <div class="container">
    <div class="row">
      <div class="s12 m6">
        <h5>Footer Content</h5>
        <p>You can use rows and columns here.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="s12 m6">
        <h5>Links</h5>
        <ul>
          <li><a href="/link-1">Link 1</a></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
    <small>
      <span>&copy; 2026 Copyright Text</span>
    </small>
  </div>
</footer>
`} />
        <p>
          Give the trailing <code>&lt;small&gt;</code> two children, the notice
          and the trailing link. It is the copyright bar, a wrapping flex row
          with space-between, so you do not need a <code>right</code> float.
        </p>
  </Section>
  <Section {...S["sticky-footer"]}>
        <p>
          For a sticky footer, add these rules to your own stylesheet once the
          page has <code>header</code>, <code>main</code> and <code>footer</code>
          landmarks. Expressive does not include them. A sticky footer sits at
          the bottom of a short page and moves down when the content is taller.
          It is not a fixed footer.
        </p>
<Code code={`
body {
  display: flex;
  min-height: 100dvh;
  flex-direction: column;
}

main {
  flex: 1 0 auto;
}
`} />
  </Section>
</PageBody>
</DocsLayout>
